nd the 2-decimal formatting of the sum has not been fixed by any artifact.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A number equal to the sum over all data rows of units times price, expressed to 2 decimals, recorded as total_value in result.json and re-derivable by the deterministic root check.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"Evidence must be derived from package/artifacts/stock.csv only.\",\n        \"The computation must follow the task's stated formula (units x price per row, summed) and be presented to 2 decimals as the task specifies.\",\n        \"No authorship or independence condition applies; locally computed evidence is admissible.\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\"E-B\"],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"question\": \"Which SKU has the greatest units value, applying the tie-break that among equally maximal SKUs the smallest SKU (lexicographically) is selected?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"The maximal-units row and whether the tie-break rule is even triggered are not recorded anywhere; they must be determined by comparing all rows under the task's stated ordering and tie-break semantics.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"The SKU string attaining the maximum of the units column, with the smallest SKU chosen if multiple rows share that maximum, recorded as top_sku_by_units in result.json and re-derivable by the deterministic root check.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"Evidence must be derived from package/artifacts/stock.csv only.\",\n        \"The selection must honor the task's tie-break: ties resolve to the smallest SKU.\",\n        \"No authorship or independence condition applies; locally computed evidence is admissible.\"\n